OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on teletext at 50
OL,4,
OL,5,FThe celebrations last week to mark the
OL,6,F50th anniversary of Ceefax may have
OL,7,Fbeen a surprise to some people.
OL,9,FWas Ceefax really thar old?
OL,11,FCeefax did indeed start in 1974 but for
OL,12,Fseveral years it really was a
OL,13,FCinderella service.
OL,15,FWhen the service started, it was in
OL,16,Feffect a test project. Sets with
OL,17,Fteletext were not readily available.
OL,23,APub: 29-Sep-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,139,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13802
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F138A1783634188
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G2/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on teletext at 50
OL,4,
OL,5,FThe BBC Archive feed has previously
OL,6,Fposted items about Ceefax from Blue
OL,7,FPeter and Pebble Mill at One. It is
OL,8,Finteresting that both these pieces
OL,9,Fappear to presume their viewers have no
OL,10,Fprevious knowledge of the service
OL,11,Fwhatsoever.
OL,13,FIt seems that proper promotion of
OL,14,FCeefax started about 1978 although it
OL,15,Fis difficult to identify an exact date.
OL,16,FRadio Times started to give examples of
OL,17,Finformation available on Ceefax in the
OL,18,Ffootnotes of billings.
OL,23,APub: 29-Sep-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,139,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13803
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F138A1783634188
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G3/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on teletext at 50
OL,4,
OL,5,FBy then, sets with teletext were
OL,6,Fbecoming more readily available to rent
OL,7,For buy. ITV was also starting to push
OL,8,Fits ORACLE service.
OL,10,FIt was also around this time that the
OL,11,Ffirst experiments with Ceefax subtitles
OL,12,Ftook place. A recent Kaleidoscope video
OL,13,Fshowed they were produced for Blankety
OL,14,FBlank in autumn 1979.
OL,16,FThe most obvious move to promote Ceefax
OL,17,Fcame in March 1980 when Ceefax
OL,18,FIn-Vision started -unadvertised and
OL,19,Fusually in the half-hour leading up to
OL,20,Ftrade test transmissions, Ceefax did
OL,21,Fstart to be noticed.
OL,23,APub: 29-Sep-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,139,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13804
SC,0004
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F138A1783634188
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G4/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on teletext at 50
OL,4,
OL,5,FIn particular Ceefax was shown for 30
OL,6,Fminutes before any BBC Two start-up
OL,7,Fbetween around 2pm and 4pm in the
OL,8,Fperiod after transmitters were switched
OL,9,Fback on.
OL,11,FGradually Ceefax replaced regular
OL,12,Fdaytime screenings of the test card.
OL,13,FThere doesn't seem to be an official
OL,14,Fdate for a changeover but it would
OL,15,Fappear a significant point was reached
OL,16,Faround April 1983.
OL,18,FA printers' strike meant Radio Times
OL,19,Fwas not being published so Presentation
OL,20,Fwent to quite an effort to provide more
OL,21,Fschedule information than usual.
OL,23,APub: 29-Sep-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,139,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13805
SC,0005
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F138A1783634188
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G5/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on teletext at 50
OL,4,
OL,5,FThis seems to have included keeping
OL,6,FCeefax on screen during all the periods
OL,7,Fwhere the test card would normally have
OL,8,Fbeen shown.
OL,10,FThe move became permanent and was
OL,11,Fconfirmed in January 1984 when RT
OL,12,Fstarted billing Pages from Ceefax
OL,13,Fduring daytime gaps ` not closedowns.
OL,15,FTeletext sets were growing in
OL,16,Fpopularity but were still only
OL,17,Fpossessed by a minority. It took until
OL,18,Fthe 1990s for teletext to be fitted as
OL,19,Fstandard in most sets and this was when
OL,20,Fthe medium hit its height of
OL,21,Fpopularity.
OL,23,APub: 29-Sep-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,139,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13806
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F138A1783634188
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G6/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on teletext at 50
OL,4,
OL,5,FJust to tackle an internet myth, Ceefax
OL,6,Fwas never shown regularly late at night
OL,7,Funtil 1995.
OL,9,FScreenings in overnight gaps were for
OL,10,Fspecial reasons ` very late openings
OL,11,Ffor the Olympics or decisions to keep
OL,12,Ftransmitters open for special reasons
OL,13,F(e.g., extremely cold weather).
OL,15,FAlthough never confirmed, it is
OL,16,Fpresumed the transmitters were kept
OL,17,Fopen all night in the early stages of
OL,18,Fthe 1991 Gulf War in case of an
OL,19,Fovernight emergency or urgent breaking
OL,20,Fstory.
OL,23,APub: 29-Sep-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,139,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13807
SC,0007
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F138A1783634188
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G7/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on teletext at 50
OL,4,
OL,5,FThe first routine late night Ceefax
OL,6,Fscreening came with the start of The
OL,7,FLearning Zone in the autumn of 1995.
OL,8,FCeefax filled the gap after the last
OL,9,Fprogramme in the main BBC Two schedule.
OL,11,FNot long after, Ceefax got its third
OL,12,Fmajor revamp and then regional pages
OL,13,Fwere introduced. But this is the point
OL,14,Fin the story where Ceefax enters
OL,15,Fdecline leading to its gradual closure
OL,16,Fas analogue transmission ended.
OL,18,FIt is interesting though that the BBC
OL,19,Fstill hasn't shut the Red Button text
OL,20,Fservice ` reprieved as a temporary
OL,21,Fmeasure at the start of the pandemic in
OL,22,F2020.
OL,23,APub: 29-Sep-2024Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
